Incident Report: Multi-Stage Linux Endpoint Compromise (MTS-Web)

Severity: High
Status: Confirmed True Positive
Environment: Linux (Unmanaged Endpoint)

1. Executive Summary

On January 15, 2026, an unauthorized remote sign-in occurred on the unmanaged Linux endpoint MTS-Web using valid credentials associated with the account newuser. The attacker authenticated from external IP 164.92.218.170 and executed a multi-stage attack involving remote access tooling, privilege escalation, malware deployment, and defense evasion.

The activity chain demonstrates a structured compromise lifecycle consistent with real-world intrusion behavior and required immediate containment and Tier 2 escalation.

2. Incident Overview

Initial Access: Successful remote authentication using valid credentials

Execution: Suspicious scripts and attacker-controlled binaries executed from world-writable directories

Privilege Escalation: Elevated processes observed consistent with system-level access

Defense Evasion: Deletion of binaries, removal of execution paths, hidden file usage

Malware Activity: Multiple detections tied to the same device and timeline

This incident reflects a deliberate, multi-phase intrusion rather than isolated malicious execution.

3. Indicators of Compromise (IOCs)

External Source IP: 164.92.218.170

Unauthorized login to unmanaged host: MTS-Web

Suspicious binaries executed from world-writable directories

Multiple deleted sshd processes

Elevated process execution following authentication

Malware alerts correlated to attack timeline

