5. Technical Findings

Authentication logs confirmed external access from a non-corporate IP.

Attacker executed payloads from world-writable directories — a common tactic for stealth execution.

Evidence of privilege escalation indicated system-level access was obtained.

Deleted sshd processes suggest temporary remote access tooling.

Malware detections align with attacker execution timeline.

The attack demonstrates intent to establish covert persistence and maintain elevated access.

